<h2><a name="Abstract">Abstract</a></h2>

<p>The HyperText Markup Language (HTML) is a simple markup language used to create
hypertext documents that are portable from one platform to another. HTML documents are
SGML documents with generic semantics that are appropriate for representing information
from a wide range of applications. The following specification extends HTML to support
ruby text typically used in East Asian documents. Familiarity with both HTML 4.0 [<a href="#html4">HTML4</a>]
and XML-ized HTML [<a href="#xml">HTML-XML]</a> is assumed.</p>

